  m_Name: Floor2
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  introLines: []
  casualLines:
  - You came back again. I wasn't sure you would.
  - You see, you can never escape this unless you listen to me
  - But I know you too well, you will not.
  - So instead of helping you again. I will let you try yourself and see at the end
    who is correct.
  - Maybe then you will realise why you are here in the first place.
  - Let me tell you a story.
  - '"Once upon a time, there was an elevator that brought people to every floor.'
  - A person named A stepped inside, pressed a button, and let the doors close.
  - "It felt ordinary at first. But one day, the elevator stopped at a floor A didn\u2019t
    recognize. The doors slid open to a narrow hallway, dimly lit, silent. The walls
    seemed to hum faintly, like a memory trying to speak."
  - A walked. At the far end, a figure waited. Always waiting. Watching.
  - "The first time, A didn\u2019t notice it, not really. Just a shadow in the corner
    of their eye. But over the days, every time the elevator opened to that floor,
    the figure was there. Sometimes a man, pale and still. Sometimes a young girl,
    small and trembling. Other times, a shape that wasn\u2019t human at all, limbs
    too long, posture impossible."
  - "It never approached. It didn\u2019t speak. But it stared. Always watching."
  - But one day, it moved. Not toward A, but in a sudden, precise way, pointing,
    tilting, turning forcing A to meet its gaze.
  - "A felt a pull, a strange urgency in that gaze. Something it wanted A to see.
    Something to remember. Something forgotten, hidden in the edges of A\u2019s mind."
  - Every day, the figure became more deliberate. It traced shapes in the air, pressed
    hands to the wall, left scratches and marks. It whispered through the silence,
    soft, insistent, though A could never hear the words clearly. Yet A felt the
    meaning, the urgency, like a pulse against their ribs.
  - 'A began to notice patterns. A sequence of numbers scratched into the walls.
    Symbols drawn in the dust. A faint melody that played in the hum of the lights. '
  - Each clue pulled at the edges of memory, unlocking fragments of a night they
    could barely recall.
  - And then one day, the figure was closer than ever. A could see the grief in its
    posture, the pleading in its eyes or whatever passed for eyes.
  - "A realized, with a cold, sinking certainty, that the figure wasn\u2019t just
    waiting, it had been waiting for them. Waiting for A to remember, to see the
    truth."
  - The hallway pulsed with unspoken urgency. Something had happened. And A was involved"
  - ..
  - ..
  - ..
  - I suppose you don't take me seriously, do you? You didn't even listen to my story
    at all.
  - Because if you did, you could have figured it out already.
  - Fine... let me ask you a question.
  - Who do you think A is?
  - 'Okay, fine maybe i should shut up. '
  - .
